.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- move files using colon-path atomic names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SOURCE DEST
.br
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SOURCE
\&...
.I DIRECTORY
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path wrapper around
.BR mv (1).
It rewrites path arguments, creates missing parent directories for
destinations, then executes
.BR mv .
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7)
for
.BR BASE:LEAF
syntax.
.PP
When the destination is a directory (or multiple sources are given), each
source is placed at
.I DEST/LEAF
where
.I LEAF
is the atomic name of the source (the part after
.BR : ,
or the basename if no colon-path was used).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ a/b:c/d ../x
Runs
.B mv a/b/c/d ../x/c/d
after creating
.BR ../x/c .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the rewritten
.B mv
command without executing it.
.PP
All other options are passed through to
.BR mv (1).
This page only lists wrapper options; see the original manual for the complete
set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mv (1),
.BR colon-path (7),
.BR colon-cp (1)
